T09:35:35Z"},"comments":5,"created_at":"2024-10-25T19:12:12Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T05:36:18Z","closed_at":"2024-11-18T15:30:03Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nMaster (4.4.dev.gh [6732a0fd8])\r\n4.3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev (6732a0fd8) - Windows 10.0.19045 - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 Ti with Max-Q Design (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.5612) - AMD Ryzen 7 3750H with Radeon Vega Mobile Gfx (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nTested this simple wireframe shader:\r\n```glsl\r\nshader_type spatial;\r\nrender_mode wireframe;\r\nuniform vec3 line_color = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\nvoid vertex() {}\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n    ALBEDO = line_color;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**It renders inconsistently in the renderers:**\r\nI suspect that Forward+ looks wrong due to a bug, possibly hardware specific. \r\nCompatibility may not work at all due to an undocumented limitation. The spatial shader docs for the `wireframe` render mode only say \"Geometry draws using lines.\", and make no mention of renderer limitations.\r\n\r\n**Forward+. Hard to see, but there are red firelies within the black.**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_VYdb63Y79v](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6910dd3f-9ff9-440d-9070-081b1534c0f4)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1f00d3ad-63e7-46fa-995a-fe907a1d2eca\r\n\r\n**Mobile:**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_ST6W4tB9BX](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8447704a-e5ca-41b8-993c-1c6e61c0b60c)\r\n\r\n**Compatibility:**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_ymLhaglzHH](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0a1ddb0-e545-4d46-8203-8ae12b580103)\r\n\r\n**The `Display Wireframe` option does work in all three renderers:**\r\n**Forward+:**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_IKQYLnt73t](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eeff30ed-699f-45b5-8f43-ea6180bb0e3c)\r\n\r\n**Mobile:**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_KX2kGbp74N](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/90424ffd-dfc1-4cb7-865d-da1936036fd1)\r\n\r\n**Compatibility:**\r\n![godot windows editor x86_64_pz33ranYSk](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/323f7f1d-9942-4b79-863e-106113745cdc)\r\n\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd a `MeshInstance3D` with a capsule mesh. Give it a `ShaderMaterial` with this shader. Try the various renderers.\r\n```glsl\r\nshader_type spatial;\r\nrender_mode wireframe;\r\nuniform vec3 line_color = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);\r\nvoid vertex() {}\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n    ALBEDO = line_color;\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://ap